# `oxfmt` reads this file. `src/low/generated/**` is codegen output from
# `@hey-api/openapi-ts` (`pnpm generate`) — reformatting it would make the
# committed files diverge from a fresh regeneration byte-for-byte, which is
# exactly what `scripts/check-spec-drift.mjs` compares. Keep it untouched,
# the same way the Python SDK excludes its generated models from `ruff`.
src/low/generated/

# Generated by `pnpm sync:python-surface`, and compared byte-for-byte against a
# fresh extraction by `scripts/sync-python-surface.mjs` (the `sdk-parity` CI
# job). Same reason as above: oxfmt collapses its short arrays, which would put
# `pnpm format:check` and the parity freshness check permanently at odds.
parity/python-surface.json

# `CLAUDE.md` is a fixed Claude Code shim whose two-line content is the org-wide
# canonical form (byte-identical across every repo). oxfmt would insert a blank
# line before the `@AGENTS.md` import, diverging this repo's shim from that
# standard; exclude it so the canonical bytes stay put. Edit AGENTS.md, not this.
# Leading slash on purpose: this file uses gitignore syntax, where a bare
# `CLAUDE.md` would match at any depth and quietly exempt a future nested shim
# too. Anchor it to the root file this comment is about.
/CLAUDE.md
